# UI Component Standardization Rules

## Overview

All UI components (buttons, text, forms) MUST use standardized components from **`Client/packages/ui/`** (import via `packages/ui`, `@/components/ui`, or `@ui` per `Client/tsconfig.base.json`). Custom implementations are FORBIDDEN unless explicitly approved.

## Standardized Components

### Layout Primitives (Box / View)

- **Use a unified layout primitive** (e.g. `Box` or `View`) for block-level layout instead of raw `<div>` or framework-specific containers. `<div>` (block) vs RN `<View>` (flex column by default) is a major source of layout bugs when sharing or migrating code.
- **Rule:** Prefer a shared `Box` (or equivalent) that standardizes flex defaults and behavior across web and (when present) React Native, so one mental model applies and moving folders does not break layout.

### Buttons

**Location**: `Client/packages/ui/components/button/`

**Available Components**:
- `Button` - Main button component with variants (primary, secondary, outline, ghost, danger, success, warning, cancel)
- `CancelButton` - Standardized cancel button (wrapper around Button with outline/ghost variant)
- `CloseButton` - Standardized close button with X icon (for modals/dialogs)
- `IconButton` - Icon-only buttons
- `CircularButton` - Circular button variant
- `NavigationButton` - Link-like navigation buttons
- `NavigationButtons` - Navigation button groups
- `RefreshButton` - Specialized refresh button

**Rules**:
- ❌ NEVER create custom `<button>` elements with inline className styles
- ❌ NEVER use raw button elements with custom padding, colors, or hover states
- ✅ ALWAYS use `Button` component for standard buttons
- ✅ ALWAYS use `CancelButton` for cancel actions
- ✅ ALWAYS use `CloseButton` for closing modals/dialogs
- ✅ ALWAYS use `IconButton` for icon-only buttons
- ✅ ALWAYS import from `packages/ui` (barrel), `@/components/ui`, or `@ui` — not ad-hoc paths under `apps/web`

**Examples**:

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG: Custom button implementation
<button
  onClick={handleClick}
  className="px-4 py-2 bg-blue-500 text-white rounded hover:bg-blue-600"
>
  Click me
</button>

// ✅ CORRECT: Use Button component
import { Button } from "../ui";

<Button variant="primary" size="md" onClick={handleClick}>
  Click me
</Button>

// ❌ WRONG: Custom cancel button
<button
  onClick={onCancel}
  className="px-4 py-2 border border-gray-300 bg-white rounded hover:bg-gray-50"
>
  Cancel
</button>

// ✅ CORRECT: Use CancelButton
import { CancelButton } from "../ui";

<CancelButton onClick={onCancel} size="md">
  Cancel
</CancelButton>

// ❌ WRONG: Custom close button
<button onClick={onClose} className="absolute right-2 top-2 text-gray-400">
  <X className="w-5 h-5" />
</button>

// ✅ CORRECT: Use CloseButton
import { CloseButton } from "../ui";

<CloseButton onClick={onClose} size="sm" className="absolute right-2 top-2" />
```

### Text Components

**Location**: `Client/packages/ui/components/text/`

**Available Components**:
- `Title` - Heading component (sizes: sm, md, lg, xl)
- `Subtitle` - Subtitle component (sizes: xs, sm, md, lg)
- `BodyText` - Body text component (sizes: xs, sm, md, lg)
- `Label` - Form label component

**Rules**:
- ❌ NEVER use direct text size classes (`text-xs`, `text-sm`, `text-base`, `text-lg`, etc.) on semantic elements
- ❌ NEVER use `<h1>`, `<h2>`, `<h3>` with custom className text sizing
- ❌ NEVER use `<p>` with custom className text sizing
- ✅ ALWAYS use `Title` component for headings (h1-h6)
- ✅ ALWAYS use `Subtitle` component for subtitles
- ✅ ALWAYS use `BodyText` component for paragraph text
- ✅ ALWAYS use `Label` component for form labels
- ✅ Use `as` prop on Title to maintain semantic HTML (e.g., `as="h1"`)

**Reference text (actual copy to show)** — Use real user-facing copy in components, not code or placeholder keys:
- **Title**: e.g. "Find your next home", "Preferences", "Location" (section/page headings).
- **Subtitle**: e.g. "Select your preferences and let our AI find the best homes for you."
- **BodyText**: e.g. "Your saved homes will appear here." (paragraphs, descriptions).
- **Label**: e.g. "Budget Range", "Ideal Zip Code", "Name" (form field labels; use `FIELD_LABELS` / `SECTION_TITLES` from `packages/utils/domain/profile/constants` or `t()` for i18n keys).
Never render translation keys or constant names as visible text; always pass the resolved string (e.g. `t("key")` or `FIELD_LABELS.NAME`) so the UI shows the actual reference text.

**Examples**:

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG: Direct text size classes
<h2 className="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold">My Title</h2>
<p className="text-sm text-gray-600">Body text</p>
<label className="text-sm font-medium">Label</label>

// ✅ CORRECT: Use standardized text components with actual reference text
import { Title, BodyText, Label } from "../ui";
import { SECTION_TITLES, FIELD_LABELS } from "packages/utils/domain/profile/constants";

<Title size="md" as="h2">{SECTION_TITLES.LOCATION_PREFERENCES}</Title>
<BodyText size="sm" muted>Select your preferences and let our AI find the best homes for you.</BodyText>
<Label size="sm">{FIELD_LABELS.NAME}</Label>

// ❌ WRONG: Showing code or keys as visible text
<Title>SECTION_TITLES.FINANCIAL_PROFILE</Title>
<BodyText>{'"form.description"'}</BodyText>

// ✅ CORRECT: Resolved strings only
<Title>{SECTION_TITLES.FINANCIAL_PROFILE}</Title>
<BodyText>{t("form.description")}</BodyText>

// ❌ WRONG: Custom heading with responsive classes
<h3 className="text-responsive-lg font-medium text-gray-900">
  Dialog Title
</h3>

// ✅ CORRECT: Use Title component
<Title size="lg" as="h3">Preferences</Title>
```

### Color System

**Primary color**: Primary actions and the primary button variant use **olive** (via `brand-accent`, set to olive in Tailwind). Do not use brown for buttons.

**Rules**:
- ✅ ALWAYS use brand tokens (`brand-accent`, `brand-primary`, `brand-secondary`, `brand-tertiary`) in Button and IconButton components
- ✅ Use semantic color variants (primary, secondary, danger, success, warning) instead of direct colors
- ✅ Primary/CTA color is olive; `brand-accent` is set to olive in Tailwind
- ❌ NEVER use brown for buttons; use olive or gray instead
- ❌ NEVER use direct color classes like `bg-brown`, `text-red-600` in button implementations
- ❌ NEVER mix brand tokens and direct colors inconsistently

**Examples**:

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG: Direct color usage
<button className="bg-brown text-white hover:bg-brown/90">
  Click me
</button>

// ✅ CORRECT: Use Button with variant
<Button variant="primary">Click me</Button>

// ❌ WRONG: Inconsistent color usage
<IconButton variant="primary" className="bg-olive" />

// ✅ CORRECT: Use standardized variant
<IconButton variant="primary" />
```

### Mobile Responsiveness

**Rules**:
- ✅ ALWAYS use standardized components which have built-in mobile responsiveness
- ✅ Use `size` prop on buttons (xs, sm, md, lg, xl) - components handle responsive sizing
- ✅ Use `hideTextBelow` prop on Button when text should hide on mobile
- ✅ Use responsive text components (Title, Subtitle, BodyText) which handle mobile sizing automatically
- ❌ NEVER add custom responsive classes to standardized components
- ❌ NEVER override mobile behavior with custom className

**Examples**:

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG: Custom responsive classes
<button className="px-2 py-1 text-xs sm:px-4 sm:py-2 sm:text-base">
  Click
</button>

// ✅ CORRECT: Use Button with size prop (handles responsiveness)
<Button size="sm">Click</Button>

// ❌ WRONG: Custom responsive text
<h2 className="text-lg sm:text-xl md:text-2xl">Title</h2>

// ✅ CORRECT: Use Title component (handles responsiveness)
<Title size="md">Title</Title>
```

## Import Patterns

**Always import from centralized location**:

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT: Import from ui/index
import { Button, CancelButton, CloseButton, Title, BodyText, Label } from "../ui";
// or
import { Button } from "packages/ui";
```

**Avoid direct imports from subdirectories** (unless necessary):

```typescript
// ⚠️ AVOID: Direct import from subdirectory
import Button from "../ui/button/Button";

// ✅ PREFER: Import from ui/index
import { Button } from "../ui";
```

## Migration Guide

When updating existing code:

1. **Find custom button implementations**:
   - Search for `<button` elements with className containing `px-`, `py-`, `bg-`, `border`, `rounded`
   - Replace with appropriate Button component variant

2. **Find custom text implementations**:
   - Search for `<h1>`, `<h2>`, `<h3>` with `text-*` classes → Replace with `Title`
   - Search for `<p>` with `text-*` classes → Replace with `BodyText`
   - Search for subtitle-like text → Replace with `Subtitle`

3. **Update imports**:
   - Add imports from `packages/ui` (or `@/components/ui`)
   - Remove custom button/text implementations

## Exceptions

The following are allowed exceptions (must be documented):

- Specialized button components in `packages/ui/components/button/` (e.g., `NotInterested`, `HeartSave`) - these are domain-specific
- Utility CSS classes in `packages/styles/` - these are for internal component styling
- Email templates - may use inline styles for email compatibility

## Enforcement

- All new code MUST use standardized components
- When refactoring existing code, replace custom implementations with standardized components
- Code reviews MUST check for compliance with these rules
- Linter rules should flag direct button/text implementations

## Component Reference

### Button Variants
- `primary` - Main action (uses brand-accent = olive; no brown on buttons)
- `secondary` - Secondary/cancel-style (gray: border, bg, text; no olive)
- `cancel` - Alias of secondary (gray); use for CancelButton or semantic cancel
- `outline` - Outlined button (uses brand-accent border)
- `ghost` - Minimal button (uses brand-accent text)
- `danger` - Destructive action (uses rose)
- `success` - Success action (uses brand-secondary)
- `warning` - Warning action (uses gold-muted)

**IconButton** supports: `primary`, `secondary`, `outline`, `ghost`, `danger`, `toolbar` (minimal toolbar style).

### Button Sizes
- `xs` - Extra small
- `sm` - Small
- `md` - Medium (default)
- `lg` - Large
- `xl` - Extra large

### Text Sizes
- **Title**: `sm`, `md`, `lg`, `xl`
- **Subtitle**: `xs`, `sm`, `md`, `lg`
- **BodyText**: `xs`, `sm`, `md`, `lg`

### Text reference copy (what users see)
- **Title**: Real headings (e.g. "Finances", "Housing", "Location") — use `SECTION_TITLES` or `t()` for section titles.
- **Subtitle / BodyText**: Real sentences (e.g. "Select your preferences and let our AI find the best homes for you.") — use `t()` for i18n.
- **Label**: Real field labels (e.g. "Name", "Budget Range") — use `FIELD_LABELS` or `t()`. Never show the constant name or key as the visible text.

